			<div class="content" id="post-content-4849622">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Comedy, Emotional (might be just an emotional piece)</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An email/fax is send to many foundation employees, including the O5-council that says that someone has failed in delivering the promised products and that they cant manufacture them any longer. Attached is a business card with the information of where this SCP is and the testing and containment ensues.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> &quot;Our business relationship has to come to an abruptive end before it even really began. I have no more funds and everything i try ends up in utter failure. It has been a pleasure working alongside you.&quot; is the email many high ranked SCP foundation personnel receive one day. Attached to it are the credentials of a business that went bankrupt a month ago. This SCP is located on an untouched coal reserve that has been bought by a coal mining company. The SCP is a factory which is supposed to create thaumiel SCPs and then sell them to the foundation with huge profit. This SCP is supposed to tell the story of how one individual tried bulding up a business with this idea and how this coal company ruined them by denying them access to much needed ressources because they want coal. All testing is halted until the mysterious individual is found. Will be found eventually (alive and somewhat well). Also includes testing logs of all different kinds of prototypes this SCP made.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> A story of medium length of how a SCP got made without malicious intent, made to aid the foundation. Also includes testing logs.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I m not sure if this SCP is supposed to end on a happy or on a sad note ( i want it to end happy because that rarely happens in SCP articles and i think happy endings are needed sometime). The individual who made this SCP gets employed by the foundation to improve this SCP. Researchers might get frustrated with how little progress they make, even though the original creator is helping. Might leave that last part out though.</p>

