			<div class="content" id="post-content-4849602">
									

<p>Solid concept and mostly good execution, but the tone and excesses put me off.</p>
<p>1- The excess technobable and Foundation-verse specifics get a lot of focus out of how alien Alexylva is supposed to feel. There is no reason for an MTF being involved, and specially the Foundation having a grasp and a name for exactly how Alexylva created this takes them from alien to bland. They naming Alexylva directly in the description doesn't help it, either, specially done as if this was enough to explain something;</p>
<p>2- I feel that a lot here is creative laziness. A lengthy containment that sums up to &quot;lock it up and build a wall&quot;, two instances of &quot;at the atomic level&quot; without a grasp of what it really means, use of shocking comments instead of actual tests, unnecessary details on the D-Class for an exploration that was bland and were his individuality ended up having no bearing.</p>
<p>Overall the final documents are ok, not bad, not good either.</p>

