														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4849601">
									

<p>The definitive guide on ListPages stuff is <a href="/listpages-magic-and-you">ListPages Magic and You</a>, which walks you through and explains how multi-iteration stuff works. In essence you make a couple hidden pages, then a main page with the ListPages, which pulls content from those hidden pages.</p>
<p>That guide semi-strongly advises using the <tt>order=&quot;created_at&quot;</tt> parameter, but if you'd like it to be random you can change it to <tt>order=&quot;random&quot;</tt>. In order to get your reader to reload the page, you can provide a button somewhere that contains a link to the page itself; e.g. if you page is SCP-4260 then use <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">[[[SCP-4260&#32;|&#32;Refresh&#32;page?]]]</span>.</p>
<p>This will effectively mean that the contents of your reader sees will be random and cycle through randomly upon refreshing the page. If you have any further questions feel free to reach out.</p>
<p>Edit: Yes hello I am competent op staff who understands how reply nesting works</p>

