<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Unsure</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> What if you lived life in a reality show? Then use Laugh Track 1952, you'll LOVE it.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The laugh track, used in old television shows, was created in 1936 and was dismissed in 1952 because of lashback from the public. Now, contained in Site-822, the laugh track is responsible for atleast two (2) deaths of Class-D a year. Here's how it works; A subject presses the button on top of the box, and it plays one out of four laugh tracks (SCP-XXXX-1, through SCP-XXXX-4). Once the subject has listened to the laugh track, they will start to fade out of consciousness and faint. Once awake, the laugh track will link itself into the brain for as long as the subject is alive.</p>
<p>Every once in a while, the laugh track (1-4) will go off, similar to that of a reality show. This makes the subjects life a literal reality show.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> If you like reality shows, you'll like this, that's about it.</p>

