			<div class="content" id="post-content-4849587">
									

<p>Thank you for your review. It is really insightful and helpful!</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The first issue with this is that I have difficulty taking the Foundation response seriously. The researchers have no reason to believe that just because they found a location that produces anomalies, said anomalies will be automatically useful. It also makes me skeptical that they would immediately use said anomalies to assist the Foundation in the first place; the Foundation exists to contain anomalies first, not to put them to questionable/unreliable use. As a reader, I'm also confused as to how the researchers started running tests on the items in the first place, since the effects noted aren't really instinctive (for example, how would someone know which criteria to test to determine the specific effects of the box?).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That makes sense actually. The researchers wouldnt know anything about its anomalous effects so they probably wouldnt just throw other SCPs inside it and see what happens. They also wouldn't just use unreliable barely tested SCPs to contain others so it would never get classified as Thaumiel in the first place. I will try and figure something out to fix those issues!</p>
<blockquote>
<p>…which brings me to the second major issue; I feel like there needs to be more explanation/worldbuilding behind why the warehouse behaves the way it does. I think we already have a Thaumiel location that knowingly assists the Foundation (I think it's a renovated schoolbuilding or the like; try using the Tag Search tool to find it), so what you have here just seems like a slight variation of it but without narrative context. Did the warehouse just spontaneously start existing to produce anomalies? Why does it want to help the Foundation at all?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I found the article in questions and yeah, they are kinda similar&#8230; What i could do to change that would be to make it non sapient and sentient and maybe not even a building&#8230; I just got a good idea of how to fix that! Will make another concept post.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Overall… I'm not convinced that this would be workable on the mainsite as currently presented. The Foundation personnel seem too quickly disappointed, and the warehouse itself seems shallowly developed. I think the first steps to take here would be to better develop the warehouse's history and motives so it exists as a meaningful character on its own, without needing the Foundation to give it significance.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Hmmm&#8230; Not too sure on how to addresse this problem. I need some time to think about a good backstory, but i get what you mean.</p>
<p>Thank you very much for your crit. It is really helpful!</p>

							</div>

								
					
