			<div class="content" id="post-content-4849576">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre (Optional): Action/History</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional): Basic format containment then background of SCP</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: An SCP item that gives the wearer invincibility inhumane strength and expansive knowledge of combat and war strategy. It comes in the form of a suit of spartan armor that will transform into whatever armor the wearer knows of.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: The armor was discovered during the Vietnam war and captured by the Foundation they then found through testing and a few containment incidents the basic abilities of the armor as well as learning with untrained individuals it will cause them to enter a blood rage upon putting it on and it will deteriorate their body killing them within hours of exposure. With individuals trained extensively in combat the blood rage will not take hold unless under extreme emotional or physical stress and the armor will deteriorate much slowly causing death much later (possibly years) than other subjects. The armor is permitted to be used in world ending situations and large site containment breaches. The armor also has access to famous warrior throughout history and the deterioration seen in subjects is most likely due to this effect as the armor will steal and contain your spirit. It also has a calling effect that pulls nearby personnel into attempting to wear it resulting in their deaths. The armor was originally created during the Battle of Thermopylae when a Persian soldier donned the armor of Leonidas causing his spirit to put a curse on the armor (causing the effects seen today).</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: This SCP is a tool the Foundation can use to combat many of the threats the Foundation faces however it is a very unstable tool and finding a suitable subject is incredibly difficult as most will die within hours, also it creates an effect similar to the &quot;One Ring&quot; from Lord of the Rings in which it pulls people towards it and typically has them fight over the owner of the armor which is very dangerous as many valuable Foundation assets could be drawn to it and die to the wearer. Also the amount of knowledge the armor holds from its past users could prove useful to the Foundation as well as its extensive knowledge of strategy.</p>
<p>Additional Notes: I feel as if I am missing something to make this story truly unique and I hope someone can take notes on this and help me figure out how to properly narrow down my ideas or give it an extra hook of some sort.</p>

